WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/vehicles/components/BatteryComparison.tsx — the "Fleet Battery Status" panel:
    BatteryComparison({ vehicles }) reads useTranslation('vehicles') + useUnits().formatDistance and runs
    ONE useQuery (queryKey ['fleet-battery-states', ids]) that fans out fetchVehicleState(v.id) per
    vehicle (refetchInterval 30_000), mapping each to { vehicle, state|null }. bars = entries whose
    state !== null; if bars.length === 0 it returns null.
      GlassPanel(p-5) → h3[ Activity icon (text-cyan-400)
                            + t('fleet.batteryStatus','Fleet Battery Status') ]
                      → div.space-y-3 → per bar:
                          span.w-24.truncate (display_name || vin)
                          div.h-3.rounded-full track → inner fill
                              width: `${level}%`  (level = battery_level ?? 0)
                              background: linear-gradient(90deg, ${color}80, ${color})
                              boxShadow: 0 0 10px ${color}40           (color = batteryColor(level))
                          span.w-10 `${level}%`
                          span.w-16 formatDistance(rated_range ?? 0)
  Helpers: batteryColor(level) = >60 #10b981(GOOD) / >25 #f59e0b(WARN) / else #ef4444(BAD) (lib/colors.ts).
           formatDistance(meters, pref, {precision}) → SI metres → km/mi, DEFAULT_PRECISION.distance = 1,
           `${formatNumber(value, locale, digits)} ${unit}`, em-dash sentinel for non-finite
           (lib/unitConversion.ts; useUnits delegates here). battery_level + rated_range are SI off the
           vehicle state; only rated_range is routed through the unit facade.

